# The day as each one lives it (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): calls and remarks to no one, by where they are in
# their day (before work, at it, done, a day off), the kind of day (market, Restday, a festival) as it falls on them,
# the hour, and their errands, the road and the watch. Then how they are: hurt, grieving, hungry, roofless, in debt,
# flush. Barks have cooldowns, so a habit shows without wearing thin. Drafts (phase 7), to tune by ear.

## The working day

rule day_late_for_work
when concept=bark shift=before here.time=dawn
cooldown 12h
say Late. Late, late, late. | If I run I'll make it. | Not a crumb of breakfast. Again.

rule day_off_to_work
when concept=bark shift=before
cooldown 12h
say Another day, another #money#. | Right. Off we go. | #work.capitalize# won't do itself.

rule day_done
when concept=bark shift=after
cooldown 12h
say Done! Done for the day. | That's me finished. | #home.capitalize#, and my feet up.

rule day_done_tired
when concept=bark shift=after tired=yes
cooldown 12h
say Every bone. Every single bone. | I could sleep standing. | Straight to #bed#. Straight there.

rule day_day_off
when concept=bark shift=day_off
cooldown 12h
say No #work# today. Not a stroke. | What shall I do with myself? | Lovely. Lovely, lovely day off.

rule day_working_hard
when concept=bark working=yes shift=during tired=yes
cooldown 6h
say How long till dusk? | My back's done in. | Keep at it. Keep at it.

rule day_working_restday
when concept=bark working=yes here.day=rest
cooldown 1d
say Working on Restday. The gods'll have words. | Everyone at chapel but me. | Somebody's got to.

rule day_working_festival
when concept=bark working=yes here.day=festival
cooldown 1d
say Everyone feasting but me. | Save me a cake, somebody! | I can smell the roasting from here.

rule day_working_market
when concept=bark working=yes here.day=market role!=merchant
cooldown 1d
say Market day, and I'm stuck at #work#. | Can't even get to the stalls. | Somebody buy me a pie.

rule day_devout_restday
when concept=bark here.day=rest piety=devout
cooldown 1d
say Chapel at noon. Don't be late. | A blessed Restday to you all. | Rest, and give thanks.

rule day_festival_merry
when concept=bark here.day=festival humour=merry here.festival
cooldown 6h
say Happy #here.festival#! | #here.festival#! Have you had a cake yet? | Dance with me! It's #here.festival#!

rule day_festival_poor
when concept=bark here.day=festival wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say Feasts are for them as can pay. | All this food and I can't touch it. | A festival. Lovely. For some.

## The hours

rule day_dawn_old
when concept=bark here.time=dawn stage=old
cooldown 1d
say Up before the birds. Always am. | At my age you don't sleep, you wait. | Another morning. Thank the gods.

rule day_dusk_lamps
when concept=bark here.time=dusk here.place=street
cooldown 12h
say Lamps soon. | Getting dark early. | Home before the light goes.

rule day_night_street
when concept=bark here.time=night here.place=street stage!=young
cooldown 12h
say Should be abed. | Dark as a pocket out here. | Mind the gutter. Mind the... ow.

rule day_night_nervy
when concept=bark here.time=night temper=nervy here.weather!=indoors
cooldown 12h
say Who's there? ... Nobody. Nobody. | I don't like the dark. Never have. | Was that a step? That was a step.

rule day_night_tavern
when concept=bark here.time=night here.place=tavern
cooldown 6h
say One more. Just the one. | Who's buying? Not me. | Another song! Another!

## Errands, the road, the watch

rule day_errand_letter
when concept=bark errand=letter
cooldown 6h
say Letter. Letter for... where is that door? | Mind out, letter to deliver. | Now who was this for?

rule day_errand_caravan
when concept=bark errand=caravan
cooldown 6h
say The caravan won't wait! | Coming, coming! | Is that them gone already?

rule day_errand_goods
when concept=bark errand=goods
cooldown 6h
say Mind your backs! Coming through! | Heavy, this. Mind out. | Watch your toes!

rule day_errand_order
when concept=bark errand=order
cooldown 6h
say An order to fetch. Don't stop me. | They wanted it yesterday. | Quick, quick.

rule day_errand_wedding
when concept=bark errand=wedding
cooldown 6h
say A wedding! Have you seen the bride? | Off to a wedding. Do I look all right? | Flowers! I forgot the flowers.

rule day_errand_funeral
when concept=bark errand=funeral
cooldown 6h
say ... | They were good folk. | Walk soft. There's been a death.

rule day_travelling
when concept=bark travelling=yes
cooldown 6h
say Long road yet. | My paws. My poor paws. | Is it far now? It's always far.

rule day_watch_night
when concept=bark on_watch=yes here.time=night
cooldown 3h
say All's well! | Who goes there? | Keep to the lamps, now.

rule day_watch_day
when concept=bark on_watch=yes here.time=dawn|day|dusk
cooldown 3h
say Move along, nothing to see. | Keep it civil, now. | Eyes open. Always.

## How they are

rule day_rich
when concept=bark wealth=rich here.place=street|market
cooldown 1d
say Out of the way, if you please. | Such crowds. | Where is that boy with my parcels?

rule day_heights
when concept=bark quarter=heights here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say One does so tire of the Commons' smell. | Ghastly crowds today. | Mind the hem. This was dear.

rule day_sump
when concept=bark quarter=sump here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say Up to the ankles again. | Sump water. Sump everything. | The Heights never smell this.

rule day_hungry
when concept=bark hungry=yes
cooldown 6h
say #hungry.capitalize#. | Spare a crust? Anyone? | I can smell bread. Torture.

rule day_homeless
when concept=bark homeless=yes
priority 1
cooldown 6h
say Anywhere dry. Anywhere at all. | Spare a corner? | Another night out, then.

rule day_on_dole
when concept=bark on_dole=yes
cooldown 1d
say Parish loaf again. | Queue's longer every week. | Thank the gods for the dole, I suppose.

rule day_owes
when concept=bark owes=yes
cooldown 1d
say If anyone asks, I'm not here. | Pay it back Restday. Restday for sure. | How did it get so much?

rule day_hurt_light
when concept=bark injured=light
cooldown 6h
say *winces* | Mind the paw. | Still #hurt#. It'll pass.

rule day_mourning_friend
when concept=bark mourning=friend
cooldown 12h
say They'd have liked this weather. | Gone. Just like that. | I keep seeing them in the crowd.

rule day_widowed
when concept=bark widowed=yes
cooldown 1d
say We used to walk here. | Quiet, without them. | #dear.capitalize#. I still say it.

rule day_fought
when concept=bark fought=yes
cooldown 6h
say Let them try again. Let them. | My jaw. My poor jaw. | Should've seen it coming.

rule day_fighting
when concept=bark fighting=yes
priority 3
say Come on, then! | Is that all? | You'll regret that!

rule day_apprentice
when concept=bark apprentice=yes working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Yes, master. Coming, master. | Sweep, fetch, carry. Sweep, fetch, carry. | One day it'll be my shop.

rule day_master
when concept=bark master=yes working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Not like that. Like this! | Where's that apprentice got to? | In my day we learnt by watching.

rule day_ambitious
when concept=bark drive=ambitious working=yes
cooldown 1d
say One day this'll all be mine. | Faster. There's money in faster. | Mark me: I'll be someone.

rule day_chatty_alone
when concept=bark self.talk=chatty
cooldown 1d
say Talking to myself again. Best company. | Nobody to talk to. Well, there's me. | Where's everyone gone?

rule day_dry
when concept=bark humour=dry here.weather=rain|storm|fog
cooldown 1d
say Lovely day for it. | Ah. Summer. | Just how I like it.
